      "extracellular": true,
      "functional_impact_measured": "Glutamate uptake: GLT1-SEP showed matched decreases in surface expression and transporter current in HEK cells relative to wild-type, indicating no detectable effect on glutamate uptake properties (L11). Surface display: confirmed by anti-V5/anti-HA live-cell labelling, surface biotinylation, and ELISA across multiple cell types (L6, L8, L12, L13). ER exit unaffected (L13).",
      "gene_symbol": "SLC1A2",
      "insert_after_residue": 199,
      "library": null,
      "linker": null,
      "loop_run_position": null,
      "median_conservation": null,
      "numbered_against": null,
      "plddt": null,
      "position_evidence": "inferred",
      "position_frame": null,
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_and_function -> surface_only (paper reports surface: yes, function: not_reported). Paper (PMID 35434559): \"Mouse GLT-1a cDNA with V5 and HA epitope tag inserted into the extracellular loop of the transporter (between Pro 199 and Pro 200)\". Audit note: Mouse GLT-1a/b (P43006): KKVLVAP|PSEEAN aligns 1:1 with human KKVLVAP|PPDEEAN, so P199|P200 is the same residue number in human (offset 0). V5/HA (from Peacey 2009) and BBS tags at this junction in this paper; no SEP/pHluorin GLT-1 construct found in this paper. Surface: biotinylation and live BTX-555 labeling of GLT-1a-BBS. Function is only cited ('silent in terms of ... structure and function (Peacey et al., 2009)'), not measured here.] L3\u2013L5 and L11 all name Pro199/Pro200 as the exact junction in mouse GLT-1a/b, the direct ortholog of human EAAT2 (SLC1A2); this is classified 'inferred' because the tag was placed in the mouse protein, not human EAAT2 directly. Python confirms that human EAAT2 canonical sequence has P at position 199 (seq[198]='P') and P at position 200 (seq[199]='P'), so the junction is structurally identical. The site lies 57 aa from the upstream TM boundary and 39 aa from the downstream TM start, both well beyond the \u22653-residue minimum. Four distinct tag types (V5, HA, BBS, SEP) have been tolerated here across at least three independent laboratories, providing unusually strong convergent evidence. Mouse GLT-1a/b (Slc1a2, the direct mouse ortholog of human SLC1A2) expressed in COS cells, primary astrocytes, and HEK-293 cells; V5, HA, BBS (bungarotoxin-binding sequence), and SEP (superecliptic pHluorin) tags each inserted between Pro199 and Pro200 in the large extracellular loop by PCR (L3, L4, L5, L11). Multiple independent laboratories used these constructs for surface-trafficking, co-IP, FRAP, and single-particle-tracking studies (L6\u2013L9, L12, L13).",
